import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 655 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 656 | 2026-10-25 | **Touch and expression, and Pieces, organised on the Home (her 15:45, 'balance it, fill it in'; the curriculum plan's step 3 on decision 5's recommendation).** Built on row 655. The four concepts that only led to the Toolbox now open Home groups of lessons, in the plan's order, whole to detail, each group with its chapter's questions: Touch: Dynamics (sdy-pf, sdy-ladder, sdy-hair, hairpin, tmx-vol, dyn-order; dynamics questions), Touch (sdy-touch, sdy-tie, tmx-touch, touch-lengths, touch-ear; dynamics from level 4, articulation), The pedals (sps-pedals, pedal), Ornaments (ornaments, grace-write). Tempo and character: Tempo (stm-sf, stm-words, stm-read, stm-metro, stm-steady, tmx-speed, tmx-change, speed-change; tempo questions), Terms (tmx-build, tmx-map, term-mixer, term-cards, term-match, term-sort; terms questions), More about tempo (tempo-walk, tempo-race, tap-tempo, same-tune-tempo), and the metronome dial as the tool to try. Reading tunes: ssk-step, ssk-shape, ssk-read, mini-tune, tune-anatomy, hear-find, echo, sight-reading, draw-tune (reading-steps questions). Melody and form: Signs and road maps (sgn-rep, sgn-volta, sgn-dc, sgn-ds, sgn-pause, dc-ds-coda, road-map; signs), Form (fmx-*, same-or-new, binary-ternary-spot, form-shapes, rondo-refrain, form-builder; form), Melody (mlx-*, phrase-marks, question-answer, melody-sequence, complete-melody; melody). Duplicate pairs: one lesson each (sdy-tie over tie-slur, ssk-step over step-skip, stm-metro as the lesson with the metronome dial as the tool); tie-slur and step-skip stay in the Toolbox. Each of the 72 new lessons carries its floor (HOME_FLOOR, from the plan's by-topic tables); all 72 open without errors. Beside (instruments, eras) stays in the Toolbox: the Home shows the five topics only. **Asked her next:** the Beginner floor of the dollhouse: add a five-finger positions room and a listen-and-sing room, and alternate the topics (renumbers the chapters after them). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch680.py. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
